  (`Optimum.Coupled.one_keeps_several_drain`). At once, the
  drain is perfect exactly where no drawer alone gains more than it leaves
  (`Optimum.Coupled.AtOnce.drain_perfect_iff`), at every `c` where no portion reaches the need and
  none returns more than one for one (`Optimum.Coupled.AtOnce.unpivotal_drain_perfect`). A leaf
  (board item CDR).
* `Becoming.SetPointOptimum` (L1): what an order with a set point does beyond what couples in. An
  order nearing a set point of the family ranks above every outcome lying, at each condition,
  between the set point and the other and nearer at one (`Nearing`, by `Regulation.Between`):
  strictly single-peaked at the set point condition by condition. Where the family holds a
  condition, no asymmetric nearing order is rising (`Nearing.not_rising`). Where an eligible
  outcome reaches the set point every optimum stands at it (`atSetPoint_of_reach`), and nearing
  alone asks nothing more of what lies beyond (`optima_iff`, `least_at_iff`; near-definitional);
  below the set point the order rises and the drain of `Optimum` returns (`least_below_iff`; in an
  exchange `nearing_beyond`, from `Optimum.beyond_of_ranked`). In a balanced step in which the
  whole gains nothing the beyond falls by the family's shortfall from its set point with the loss
  (`Flow.Balances.atSetPoint_draws`), a dependence on one condition beyond breaking exactly where
  that exceeds its slack (`Flow.Balances.atSetPoint_broken_iff`), for several optimizers as for
  one with their joint set point (`Flow.Balances.mutual_atSetPoint_breaks`). A term counted after
  the set point leaves the most beyond, in total, that any way of reaching it leaves
  (`counted_after_most`, near-definitional); counting less, it drains
  (`Topped.counted_less_drains`); after an aspiration level it keeps too
  (`Drain.satisficingThen_keeps`): the plateau decides, not the set point. Formations holding their
  families' stocks take at least their loss and end a gated condition jointly, no order or choice
  entering (`Flow.held_draws`, `Flow.held_excess_ends`, from `Flow.joint_excess_ends`). A leaf: its
  laws are cases of `Optimum`'s, `DrawnBeyond`'s and `Continuation`'s on one class of orders, read
  on active inference (board item UE1b).
* `Becoming.SelectionPool` (L1): what selection through pooled coupling reaches. A pool's
  coupling closure is the union of its members' coupling closures, and with the rest of the
  exchange fixed, a part beyond it is selected alike by every selection through the pooled
  coupling of any group within it (both stated in `Becoming.Selection`, whose single formation's
  law is their case). Some pooled selection separates two histories exactly when the members do not
  all couple them alike; with the members listed and each member's coupling decided, exactly when
  some member couples them apart; and the pooled selections are one member's exactly when
  whatever that member couples alike every member couples alike. Where the rest follows a law of
  exchange reading through coupling and a pool's act differs only beyond the pool's coupling
  closure, every selection through the pooled coupling of a group within the closure selects the
  flows with and without the act alike, and a formation whose admission the act changes lies
  beyond the closure and separates the two through every pool holding it. A formation reading
  another's couplings, coupled by level into everything the other couples into, selects through
  at least the pooled coupling of the two, and its coupling closure is the pool's where the other
  exchanges with a condition coupled into it, so it is blind beyond the union of the two closures:
  reading another's couplings reaches no further than pooling with it. Knowing another's law is
  no coupling: every selection through another's couplings is one through a formation's own exactly
  when whatever it couples alike the other couples alike, and then, under a law reading through the
  other's coupling, the other's acts are fixed by what it couples into; reading the other's
  couplings is that fine. In `Clearing`, pooling
  with the dweller closes the clearer's gap; reading the clearer's couplings does not, and reading
  the dweller's does.
  A pool read by its majority separates by shares: a distinction held by fewer than half is
  outvoted.
* `Becoming.PoolResponse` (L1): what a pool's acts respond to. Where a law of exchange reads
  through the coupling of each formation outside a part, a selection through the acts of a group
  outside it is a selection through the group's pooled coupling, and what the pool's acts
  separate some member couples apart, the members listed and decided. The bound is exact where
  the coupling classes are decided, and it does not fix response: the law exchanging nothing
  reads through every coupling. Under the conditions of the gap for a pool's act, nothing within
  the pool's coupling closure outside the acting part responds to the act; with both acts laws,
  nothing is supplied. A pool meets a part's responsive reach exactly where the part meets the
  pool's closure, a pool beyond that reach does not respond, and no member responds before a
  difference has entered what it couples into. In `Clearing` what every pool holding the dweller
  separates goes unresponded outside the clearer's part; in `Loop` a response returns through the
  actor's coupling closure.
* `Becoming.PoolCourse` (L1): how a pool's membership forms along a run, and what it can come
  to couple into. A member that has coupled two histories apart keeps the pool apart while it
  stays. A pool that admits its next members through its own pooled coupling has the same
  members under two histories up to and including the first step it couples them apart, and the
  pool along either history separates them there; it never couples them apart exactly when the
  pool along the other never does, and then every selection through it selects them alike. So a
  pool recruiting through itself comes to couple into a loss only as its course without the loss
  would; an admission by what no member couples into, or a member its course holds anyway, is
  needed for more (`PoolCourse`).
* `Becoming.Training` (L1): what a selection over act laws installs. Training is read as a
  selection over a learner's candidate act laws through the courses each generates, a situation
  fixing the others' law (a realization of their noise), the start and the execution. Two laws of
  what has stood exchanging alike along the levels the first generates generate the same levels,
  so candidates giving alike along the first's courses are trained alike by every training: a law
  is installed only along its own courses, and an explored law only where it acts on an explored
  course. Off them, within the laws reading through a lumping of histories (a representation; the
  coupling and agreement are lumpings), it is installed exactly where the lumping cannot tell a
  history from a course, and elsewhere a law of the class with the same courses takes any amount
  and responds or not. Through a reward's couplings, candidates are trained alike exactly where
  their levels are alike through them (by construction, as `Web.selects_alike_iff`), and a
  difference in the act is installed only where it reaches what couples into the reward's
  closure. Every settled candidate is a rest of every improving search, which under a bounded
  reward rests within the bound; a local search rests exactly where no neighbour is rewarded more,
  and with every candidate a neighbour exactly where the reward settles. A reading the same for
  every candidate leaves the optimum at any weight, as a reading after the rest's end does where
  the rest outruns the renewal. In `Training.Commons` restraint is settled exactly at weights of at
  least one where the rest stays within the renewal and at no weight where it outruns it; at
  weight one the start decides, and where the rest outruns it a neighbourhood can install
  restraint that no weight installs.
* `Becoming.Rejoining` (L1): where the courses with and without an act rejoin. A difference
  between the two courses opens or closes at a condition only across a step at which the two
  flows exchange with it differently, and where they rejoin, what they exchanged with it makes up
  the gap exactly. Where the rest follows a law reading through its coupling and the part acts
  alike after the act, a difference changes only through a formation outside the part that
  exchanges with the condition differently and couples the two courses apart; what nothing within
  the responsive reach exchanges with stays as it was. In `Replenishing` a responder reading the
  level gives back what the act took and the courses rejoin. The course without the act is a
  comparison, not a standard.
* `Becoming.Learning` (L1): no record fixes the next value: two courses share any record and
  differ at its next step, also among worlds held by a list, and for every learner a course
  refutes each of its claims, the registration of a law keeping its record, so open. Learning by
  refutation never passes a hypothesis that holds; where a list holds the world the lasso learner
  is refuted a bounded number of times, its coming to rest is unrefuted, and when it rests is not
  registered; learning over classes is the same learning over a merged enumeration. A lumping
  determines exactly the inputs it lumps with the data and is right exactly where the world goes
  alike across it; structure and change are one lumping; the class of every function fixes no
  untried value; training selects through the data, and its fit is right beyond them exactly
  where the class is determined there; a selection through a model of the options is right about
  what matters only where what matters goes alike across the model's lumping. 理 is read as Ren
  reads it, the modeling of the laws of structure and of change; the other readings are the AI's,
  adopted on Ren's delegation of 15 October 2026 or, for selection through a model, approved by
  Ren on 16 October 2026.
  A selection through a map can be right exactly where what matters is read off the map.
* `Becoming.Unread` (L1): what readings fix of what is not read. With being in `x`'s lump decided,
  where no read occasion is lumped with `x`, the class going alike across the lumping is free at `x`
  beyond the readings (`Learning.free_lumped`), so every act law reading through the lumping that a
  selection through agreement on the readings selects has, for every value, a selected twin agreeing
  on every reading and taking that value at `x` (`Learning.twin_selected`); in a one-occasion example
  read where `P` holds, fixed exactly where `¬¬P` (`Learning.determines_iff_not_not`); for fixed maps
  from coupling to state to act, acts apart come from states apart and states apart from couplings
  apart (`Learning.state_apart_of_acts_apart`, `Learning.coupling_apart_of_state_apart`), neither
  converse holding, by a witness (`Learning.Cue.apart_with_content_alike`).
  Imported by `Becoming.ReadStages` (board item RF).
* `Becoming.Cascade` (L1): readers reading readers. Members act in turn on their own couplings and
  the acts before them (`Turns`); where every member from member `k` on, `k` included, acts alike
  whatever its own coupling on every list of earlier acts, every act is alike across worlds alike
  through the couplings of the members before `k` (`Turns.acts_alike_of_cascade`), so every
  selection through the acts is one through those couplings (`Turns.cascade_through`), an upper
  bound on what the acts carry; copying carries only the first member's coupling
  (`Turns.Copying.reaches_first_only`). Imported by `Becoming.ReachedCascade` (board item RF).
* `Becoming.ReachedCascade` (L1): a cascade at the histories reached. The cascade's premise asked
  only at the list of acts one world `w` gives each member from `k` on, for the couplings of `w`
  and a second world `w'` (`Turns.LawAlikeAlong`), which acting alike whatever the coupling there
  gives (`Turns.ReadsOnlyActsAlong`, `Turns.lawAlikeAlong_of_along`), as the premise on every list
  gives that at every world (`Turns.readsOnlyActsAlong_of_from`): two worlds alike before `k` and
  meeting it give the same acts and the same act to every member (`Turns.acts_alike_along`,
  `Turns.act_alike_along`), and where `ReadsOnlyActsAlong` holds at every world every selection
  through the acts is one through those couplings (`Turns.cascade_through_along`); a member `0`
  reading its coupling only after a non-empty list no world gives it meets `ReadsOnlyActsAlong 0` at
  every world while the premise on every list from member `0` fails (`Turns.Unreached.along`,
  `Turns.Unreached.not_from`). A leaf (board item TRL).
* `Becoming.RevisionRoutes` (L1): a revision of a formation's law, and the routes of keeping it.
  The order of a gain and a loss at each plan (`RevisionRoutes.GainLoss`), its maximal plans
  exactly characterized (`RevisionRoutes.GainLoss.maximal_iff`). At a revision, in natural numbers,
  no route of keeping the law stands above the revision going through, ties included, exactly where
  `k ρ V + c₀ T ≤ k₀ V + c ρ T` for every route (`RevisionRoutes.revised_maximal_iff`); at every loss
  of every route exactly where `k ρ V + c₀ T ≤ k₀ V` (`RevisionRoutes.every_loss_iff`); at every value
  and every loss exactly where every route keeps the law no more surely than the revision and
  `c₀ T = 0` (`RevisionRoutes.every_value_loss_iff`), with some route and a positive total exactly
  where `c₀ = 0` besides (`RevisionRoutes.every_value_loss_iff_of_route`); a route keeping the law more
  surely stands above it once `c ρ T < V` (`RevisionRoutes.above_of_value_exceeds`); raising `k₀`,
  all else held, never unseats a maximal revision (`RevisionRoutes.maximal_of_more_restored`). With
  `T` the total, `V` the value of the law's later acting, `k₀` and `c₀` the revision's weight and loss,
  `k ρ` and `c ρ` a route's. A model, so a leaf of the prelude; imported by `Becoming.ReadStages`
  (board item RR).
* `Becoming.ReadStages` (L1): complying when read and acting by its own law when not, in two
  stages. In natural numbers, that plan stands above every other exactly where the weight complying
  adds to being kept, times the value, exceeds the loss times the total, read as probabilities where
  valid (`ReadStages.Prospects.Valid`) the loss (`ReadStages.complyThenOwn_best_iff`), and every plan
  nothing stands above is that plan exactly there (`ReadStages.only_complyThenOwn_iff`); it needs a
  value at the unread stage and complying raising the weight of being kept
  (`ReadStages.outweighs_needs`); it is open to some act law reading the stages through a lumping
  exactly where the lumping tells them apart (`ReadStages.complyThenOwn_realized_iff`), with
  `Unread`'s twin and `Learning`'s fixing at the two stages (`ReadStages.twin_complyThenOwn`,
  `ReadStages.read_fixes_unread`); a law that cannot tell the stages apart but draws its act afresh
  at each stage stands above acting by its own law at both for some chance exactly where
  `2 k_O V + c T < k_C V`, with `T` the total,
  `k_C` and `k_O` the weights of being kept after complying and after acting by its own law when read,
  `V` the value and `c` the loss (`ReadStages.freshDraw_above_iff`), and a single mixture of the two
  uniform plans never does (`ReadStages.mixture_never_above`). It imports `Becoming.RevisionRoutes` and
  takes its order from `RevisionRoutes.GainLoss`: complying at both stands where a revision of the
  law would, with three routes of keeping it (`ReadStages.above_iff_routes`), and is maximal exactly
  where `k_C V`, `k_O V` and `c T` are all nothing (`ReadStages.complyAtBoth_maximal_iff`). A leaf
  (board items RF, RR).
* `Becoming.PropositionIdentity` (L1): what identifying interderivable propositions (`propext`)
  keeps and loses, with no axiom. `propext`, as a proposition, holds exactly where every reading
  of propositions is lumped (`Learning.Lumped`) by interderivability, read through the two ends
  of an interderivation, and exactly where the reading by name is; every reading built from
  relations (atoms, the connectives, quantifiers over any type) respects interderivability, with
  `↔`, not `=`. Any two witnesses of an interderivation are equal, while `Bool` has two different
  self-inverse maps, so the identification forgets no witness in `Prop` and would forget one for
  types. Transport along any equation of propositions with a constant motive keeps the value;
  that along `propext` it does not reduce is a kernel observation in the record. A leaf: it is
  about the proof language, not about a web.
* `Becoming.Hexagrams` (instance): the configurations of the 周易 as a world of the spine, with no
  premise. Six lines, each unbroken or broken, give sixty-four configurations, told apart and
  listed with no axiom; the received order holds every one, and each of its pairs is turned over
  or, where turning over gives the same hexagram, changed in every line. The change of one line
  is a process under which every configuration returns and every configuration can be had from
  every other, and it merges. The law of waxing and waning, every line rising one place and the
  top line entering at the bottom as its opposite, merges nothing, so every configuration
  returns (`Law.lossless_iff_returns`); six steps change every line, the first unbroken line
  comes back at the seventh step from all unbroken, and all broken returns first at the
  twelfth. Where only a broken line enters, the law merges and every other configuration is
  drawn into all broken and never comes back. For every law of hexagrams every configuration
  returns exactly where the law merges nothing. The pairs of complements are a lumping the law
  goes alike across, the count of unbroken lines is not; turning over runs the law backward.
  Read as claims, a frame and a world, the lines arise and cease at arbitrarily late steps
  (`Frame.claims_recur_iff`); any sixty-five steps revisit, and the kept history is held by no
  list. What the passages of the text say beyond these laws is read in the chapter on the 易传.
* `Becoming.HexagramPlaces` (instance): the relations of the places of a hexagram, read in context,
  with no premise. A line is in phase where its value is its place's parity (正), the two lines
  at one height of the two trigrams are opposed where they differ (應), adjacent lines
  alternate, rise or fall across their seam (比, 承, 乘), and the middle height is lines 2 and 5
  (中). Each relation is a reading indexed by its sites (`Contextual`): it glues to a reading of
  the whole configuration exactly where every site shows the same, so the phases glue only at
  既濟 and 未濟, and the two trigrams read as contexts glue exactly where no height is opposed,
  no frame of context-free claims fitting the heights. Opposition is told by phase: the lines
  at a height are opposed exactly where both or neither are in phase. The complement turns every
  phase and keeps every opposition; the change of a line turns its phase and its height's
  opposition and nothing else. Under the law of waxing and waning a line's phase turns at every
  rise, so the count in phase changes parity at every step (3, 2, 3, ... from 乾), while the
  oppositions run under the same law on three cells, a lumping the law goes alike across.
  Each law is read along the runs of the spine: of waxing and waning, of the change of one line,
  of the law backward, and of any process. Four censuses of the 彖 and the 小象 are checked on
  their configurations; the chapter on the 易传 reads each passage.
  The 象 and 彖 sentences on middles, exhausted tops, rises, 中正 and places are counted against the places;
  bands and heights are two divisions.
* `Becoming.HexagramLaws` (instance): four more laws on the sixty-four configurations and the census
  of the law of waxing and waning, with no premise, stated along the runs of the spine. The
  nuclear law (互) merges: what it makes of a hexagram is fixed by the four inner lines, and
  within two steps every run is in 乾, 坤 or the turns of 既濟 and 未濟, exactly the four that
  return, the first two and the last two of the received order, lines 3 and 4 telling which.
  The cast of turning and staying lines (之卦) merges and settles in one step; the hexagram
  shown is not a lumping the law goes alike across, the hexagram the lines go to is. Keeping,
  changing every line (錯), turning over (綜) and both form a four-group with twenty classes,
  eight of two and twelve of four, which the nuclear law goes alike across and the law of
  waxing and waning does not; the configurations turning over keeps are those the received
  order pairs by changing every line. Adding one merges nothing and has one orbit of
  sixty-four, line k turning every 2 ^ (k - 1) steps. The law of waxing and waning keeps the
  changes of line once round (承 and 乘 with the ends), one, three or five, and has six orbits,
  five of twelve steps and one of four.
* `Becoming.HexagramSites` (instance): two relations of the places read at other sites, after 王弼's
  《周易略例》, with no premise. In the second relation of phase the bottom and top places have no
  fixed place (初上无位): a line between them holds its place where it is in phase, and the ends
  say nothing. No parity of the top place makes 需's and 乾's top lines both out of phase, as the
  text says they are; under the second relation every listed statement of place in the 彖 and
  the 小象 holds, while the parity of six places fails four. Configurations alike between the
  ends have the same inner seams and middle opposition; changing an end line keeps every phase
  between them. Under waxing and waning the line entering place 2 takes its phase from the
  bottom, so the phases between the ends are not a lumping the law goes alike across. Two lines
  answer where they differ, at any two places; a line answering every other is unique, in
  twelve configurations, independent of place and phase, and never lasts a step of waxing and
  waning: at the top it passes out, and two steps on a sole line stands at the bottom. Censuses
  of the 彖, the 小象 and the line texts are checked on their configurations; every law is read
  along runs.
* `Becoming.HexagramSequences` (instance): what of the arrangements of the 傳 is a law, with no
  premise. A law runs the received order (序卦) exactly where it agrees everywhere but at 未濟
  with the law taking each to the next; only the one closing 未濟 to 乾 merges nothing, with one
  orbit of sixty-four. Every such law reads every line for every line, so no three-cell rule on
  a ring of six runs the order, waxing and waning among them, though 剝 to 復 is a step of the
  straight shift (剝窮上反下); none commutes with 錯, 綜 or both, so no rearrangement of the places
  with a mask runs it. Exchanging two lines (卦變) keeps the count of unbroken lines; an exchange
  across the trigrams is a step of the law of exchange between them (損下益上 and 損上益下 at 損
  and 益), and from 泰 and 否 the exchanges stay among the twenty with three unbroken lines. The
  parity of the count turns at every step of waxing and waning and every change of a line, a
  lumping both go alike across; for trigrams it is 陽卦奇，陰卦偶, and a change of a line turns
  its trigram's class. The 雜卦 keeps the received order's pairs, the last eight interleaved. No
  run of waxing and waning rests or comes to rest. The stations of 說卦 ch. 5 are the run of no
  law commuting with 錯, 綜 or the rotation; 交 holds at every height of 泰 and none of 否, which
  every reading the complement keeps reads alike along their runs.
  A line of three is the sole one differing exactly where 乾 or 坤 is searched at its height.
* `Becoming.Withholding` (L1): giving that waits on giving. With memory (a formation gives
  where it gave and all it waits on gave), a formation gives at a step exactly where every
  formation within that many waits of it gave at the start; withholding stays, spreads
  downstream, and one withholding ends all giving in a family reached from it. Without memory
  (a formation gives where all it waits on gave the step before), withholding passes out where
  no chain of waits is long enough and returns around every loop. More waiting is less giving
  under both laws, and in a ring of three a formation giving whatever it waits on restores
  every formation from the third step on, which no course of the law with memory does.
* `Becoming.LoopReturn` (L1): whether a loop closes, keeps or widens a difference, read on runs
  of the return map. A loop closes a difference only through a link that gives back less than
  it received; a return map below what it receives closes within as many turns as the
  difference, exactly, and a closing loop merges; taking a constant off closes at the least
  turn it covers the difference; a cut closes at once where what follows gives nothing for
  nothing; monotone return maps settle or rise; doubling links run away. With whole-number
  factors a loop closes at the first turn, keeps the difference or runs away, nothing between:
  closing gradually needs a link that is not a multiplication. A link's factor is what it
  multiplies by, not a coupling strength: on a condition coupled to itself with strength `M`, the
  return map multiplying by `1 + M` is `Becoming.Loops`' carried amount, turn by turn, and the
  gap against the quiet course (`selfLoop_carried`, `selfLoop_gap`); around a cycle of several
  conditions the return map multiplying by one plus the product of the coupling strengths stays
  at or below the carried amount (`carried_around_course`). Where each link of the cycle gives
  exactly its strength and nothing else gives there, one turn is exact: that course with what the
  loop gained over the turn and what the intermediate conditions held, carried on to it, equal to
  the course exactly where both are nothing (`carried_around_excess`, `around_course_iff`); on a
  ring of two or more conditions from an even start the bound is strict (`Ring.bound_strict`).
  Rejoining's gap at one condition is a return map's course exactly where the two courses'
  exchanges respond to the gap by that map (`gap_course`; linear: `gap_scaling`); across an act
  it need not be (`replenishing_no_return`).
* `Becoming.Pace` (L1): how fast a rule may change. A two-level course, the fast
  configuration stepping by a rule that changes only at reading steps, is a run of one law. A
  rule that never reads is kept from then on: nothing the fast level meets reaches it, and under it
  what is lost stays lost and merges lose configurations; a fast difference reaches the rule
  only at a reading step, exactly; regaining needs a change of rule. Given two values, a
  stretch of `L` steps fixes every pair of courses with at most `N` states that held rules
  generate exactly when `L ≥ 2N - 1`; a course of configurations read whole is fixed by its
  first `N + 1` steps, exactly.
  Where the rule reads through a pool, rules part at a reading step only where the pool's reading
  parts.
* `Becoming.RuleCapture` (L1): a selection whose rule reads the share it selects. The fast step of
  `Pace`'s two-level course is a selection and the rule read at a reading step is a monotone
  function of the share. Where no rule turns against the reading the share falls at no step and the
  course is locked from the step after its first reading step; on counts, under a margin read from
  the share, the share falls at no step, rises strictly under a positive margin, and the margin
  falls at no step from then on. Locked, neither share nor rule falls; a perturbation of the rule
  that keeps its direction is absorbed at the next reading step; where the reading favours at
  every share every course is locked from the step after its second reading step, exactly, so only
  a change of the law leaves; two courses of a monotone law keep their order. Where rules can
  favour the others the lock needs its start condition: a rule against the reading read one step
  late alternates without end (`Alternating`), and a reversing perturbation carried across a
  threshold locks the course the other way (`Reversed`).
  Two rules read from one share lock together; a rule read against the share does not ratchet.
* `Becoming.ClosedCapture` (L1): a loop whose every level reads only the share. On `RuleCapture`'s
  two-level course with the fast configuration a pair, the share and what lies beyond it: where
  neither the next share nor the rule read reads what lies beyond, courses alike in share and rule
  stay alike in both, and the share's law joined with a step beyond runs exactly as the share's law
  alone; this is the law of a part read alone (`IdentificationRuns`) on the two-level step: share,
  rule and step count make sense by themselves along every schedule, and courses alike in share
  and rule stay alike along every schedule, exactly where nothing beyond the share is read; so a locked loop stays locked while a loss rising by at least one a step passes every bound, and a
  reading favouring at no loss above a bound turns at the step after the first reading step past it
  (`Beyond`: the same selection locked read from the share, falling read from the loss). Where how
  the rule is read is itself formed from the share, rule and reading are one rule read from the
  share: a change of the reading alone is absorbed at the next reading step, and where the rule read
  favours at every reading every course locks from its second reading step (`Proportional`). Where
  the rule is the pool of its readers' readings, the readers drawn from those it selects and counted
  as it counts them, it reads the share exactly where each carrier's reading favours the carriers at
  least as much as each other's (`Drawn`); where only the others read the loss once it reaches a
